And I walked down to Ed's trailer and I'm just awkward in general.

1225
01:02:54.340 --> 01:03:02.100
But then also I had a bit of a fangirl thing because I loved Ed on The Daily Show and I was

1226
01:03:02.100 --> 01:03:03.960
still so excited that he was on The Office.

1227
01:03:04.120 --> 01:03:09.220
So I just awkwardly knocked on his trailer door and told him, hey, we're thinking about

1228
01:03:09.220 --> 01:03:11.280
having Andy sing, take a chance on me to Angela.

1229
01:03:12.020 --> 01:03:14.340
And we just wanted you to start thinking about the song.

1230
01:03:14.460 --> 01:03:15.080
He's like, what song?

1231
01:03:15.180 --> 01:03:16.320
I said, take a chance on me.

1232
01:03:16.700 --> 01:03:17.780
Mamma Mia, Abba.

1233
01:03:18.920 --> 01:03:21.320
And he didn't know the song.

1234
01:03:21.540 --> 01:03:24.360
And I'm thinking, oh, God, how can you not know the song?

1235
01:03:24.540 --> 01:03:27.160
Maybe slightly predicting the horror that was about to come.

1236
01:03:27.980 --> 01:03:30.160
And he's like, how does it go?

1237
01:03:30.360 --> 01:03:32.140
And I am a terrible singer.

1238
01:03:32.260 --> 01:03:33.100
I cannot sing at all.

1239
01:03:33.460 --> 01:03:38.860
And so I was like, oh, you know, it's like, remember Mamma Mia?

1240
01:03:39.320 --> 01:03:40.900
And did you know the song?

1241
01:03:41.120 --> 01:03:43.800
And I just tried to figure out how to say it without singing it.

1242
01:03:43.800 --> 01:03:50.180
And then we ended up walking around the parking lot and I had to sing Take a Chance

1243
01:03:50.180 --> 01:03:56.740
on me to Ed and it was so embarrassing, but so lovely.

1244
01:03:57.040 --> 01:03:58.600
He was so wonderful about it.

1245
01:03:58.760 --> 01:04:01.280
And I love that scene so much.

1246
01:04:01.440 --> 01:04:07.760
I just thought he killed it and was so excited that that he was able to do such a fantastic

1247
01:04:07.760 --> 01:04:08.420
job with it.

1248
01:04:08.420 --> 01:04:09.400
It was just exciting.

1249
01:04:11.340 --> 01:04:12.260
That would be me.

1250
01:04:12.420 --> 01:04:16.900
I'd be so nervous if all of a sudden I had to sing something to someone because I hate

1251
01:04:16.900 --> 01:04:17.940
singing in front of people.

1252
01:04:18.120 --> 01:04:23.060
I love to belt it out, you know, at home, in the shower or like just in the kitchen with

1253
01:04:23.060 --> 01:04:23.540
the kids.

1254
01:04:23.740 --> 01:04:31.000
But if I had to like, you know, oh, my God, like have someone like Ed or like Steve or

1255
01:04:31.000 --> 01:04:33.020
someone be like, OK, how does that go?

1256
01:04:33.180 --> 01:04:35.260
I'd be so nervous and embarrassed.

1257
01:04:36.920 --> 01:04:43.620
Well, we also got a lot of fan questions from Jen Reynolds, Sarah Thorup, Stephen Jackson,

1258
01:04:43.880 --> 01:04:45.820
Roxanne Hoffman and Becca Harrington.

1259
01:04:46.140 --> 01:04:51.080
They wanted to know who sang the backup on the telephone for Andy.

1260
01:04:51.900 --> 01:04:53.420
How was that accomplished?

1261
01:04:53.900 --> 01:04:57.140
Were they actually on the line or was it pre-recorded?

1262
01:04:57.620 --> 01:05:00.520
Oh, Jenna, my memory is we did that in real time.

1263
01:05:00.600 --> 01:05:03.340
And I'll tell you why, because I had to be there reacting.

1264
01:05:03.520 --> 01:05:08.540
And I thought, whatever you do, Angela, you cannot mess this up for these guys, you know,

1265
01:05:09.000 --> 01:05:11.680
like because they had it all timed out.

1266
01:05:11.840 --> 01:05:14.240
And we actually asked Jen Salata about it.

1267
01:05:14.340 --> 01:05:15.680
And this is what she had to say.

1268
01:05:15.880 --> 01:05:20.500
One of the singers we were so lucky to get for the acapella Take a Chance on Me was John

1269
01:05:20.500 --> 01:05:21.280
Michael Higgins.

1270
01:05:21.440 --> 01:05:23.740
You'll know him from Christopher Guest movies.

1271
01:05:24.060 --> 01:05:24.760
He's just brilliant.

1272
01:05:25.000 --> 01:05:26.460
And so we were super, super excited.

1273
01:05:26.720 --> 01:05:29.640
I don't know who the other singer was.

1274
01:05:29.640 --> 01:05:32.520
So I tried to track it down and I was unsuccessful.

1275
01:05:34.130 --> 01:05:43.260
We I believe we recorded it on the day in that John and whoever else maybe besides John

1276
01:05:43.260 --> 01:05:47.200
were in the little office that the writers used to hang out on on set.

1277
01:05:47.400 --> 01:05:50.820
And they called in and sang through the speakerphones.

1278
01:05:51.000 --> 01:05:57.720
And then I'm sure we recorded a clean version, too, of it, not through the speakerphones so that

1279
01:05:57.720 --> 01:06:03.060
we could have it in the mix and then just make sure that we got the sound quality great.

1280
01:06:03.360 --> 01:06:05.480
But it was a really fun day.

1281
01:06:05.760 --> 01:06:07.940
I just thought that they killed it.

1282
01:06:07.940 --> 01:06:14.160
Well, I remember that, Angela, because I remember listening to Ed and those guys practicing

1283
01:06:14.880 --> 01:06:20.160
before they divided up and went into the sort of speakerphone situation.

1284
01:06:20.400 --> 01:06:20.800
Right, right.

1285
01:06:21.220 --> 01:06:23.120
But it was a big deal.

1286
01:06:23.120 --> 01:06:28.380
And what a big get for just this voice on the phone that has gone completely uncredited.

1287
01:06:28.640 --> 01:06:29.320
I know.

1288
01:06:29.440 --> 01:06:31.420
And I am such a fan of John's.

1289
01:06:31.420 --> 01:06:38.260
It's like he is such a comedic genius and and and he and Ed and how they put this all

1290
01:06:38.260 --> 01:06:41.180
together and did it was so fantastic.

1291
01:06:41.700 --> 01:06:43.740
I loved every second of it.

1292
01:06:43.920 --> 01:06:49.440
It was hard for me not to fully smile because it was so charming and delightful.

1293
01:06:49.820 --> 01:06:52.640
And, you know, Angela's trying not to tip her hand too much.

1294
01:06:52.760 --> 01:06:55.980
She only has a very slight smile at like one or two parts.

1295
01:06:56.120 --> 01:06:56.300
Right.

1296
01:06:56.820 --> 01:06:56.980
Yep.

1297
01:06:56.980 --> 01:07:03.520
But I just I have such fond memories of this and I just felt like we had to hear it.

1298
01:07:03.960 --> 01:07:09.920
If you change your mind, I'll be first in line.

1299
01:07:10.500 --> 01:07:12.180
Honey, I'm still free.

1300
01:07:12.960 --> 01:07:14.520
Take a chance on me.

1301
01:07:14.920 --> 01:07:17.500
If you need me, let me know.

1302
01:07:17.600 --> 01:07:19.000
Gonna be around.

1303
01:07:19.360 --> 01:07:21.840
If you got no place to go.

1304
01:07:22.020 --> 01:07:23.480
If you're feeling down.

1305
01:07:23.480 --> 01:07:29.000
If you're all alone when the pretty birds have flown.

1306
01:07:29.000 --> 01:07:30.560
Honey, I'm still free.

1307
01:07:30.920 --> 01:07:32.980
Take a chance on me.

1308
01:07:33.600 --> 01:07:36.160
Gonna do my very beSt.

1309
01:07:36.160 --> 01:07:37.680
And that ain't no lie.

1310
01:07:37.860 --> 01:07:40.560
If you put me to the teSt.

1311
01:07:40.560 --> 01:07:42.120
If you let me try.

1312
01:07:42.380 --> 01:07:44.460
Take a chance on me.

1313
01:07:46.670 --> 01:07:48.810
That's all I ask of you, Angela.

1314
01:07:50.430 --> 01:07:54.930
I mean, I mean, come on, how they harmonize at the end like that.

1315
01:07:55.370 --> 01:07:55.770
All right.

1316
01:07:55.770 --> 01:07:57.430
I got goosebumps listening to that.

1317
01:07:57.630 --> 01:07:58.710
I got a little choked up.

1318
01:07:59.090 --> 01:08:01.990
I don't know if I just miss Ed a lot.

1319
01:08:02.110 --> 01:08:04.510
And he's so charming in this scene.

1320
01:08:04.690 --> 01:08:04.950
Yeah.

1321
01:08:05.090 --> 01:08:07.050
Or if it's just the time we're in.

1322
01:08:08.570 --> 01:08:09.590
I don't know.

1323
01:08:09.590 --> 01:08:14.330
I've also just fallen in love with Andy during this rewatch.

1324
01:08:14.710 --> 01:08:19.890
You know, we've talked about how I have this new appreciation for Ryan.

1325
01:08:20.130 --> 01:08:20.590
Right.

1326
01:08:20.750 --> 01:08:25.250
But I also just have been loving the character of Andy and his journey.

1327
01:08:26.710 --> 01:08:28.150
But I don't know, Angela.

1328
01:08:28.330 --> 01:08:34.210
I also have to say, I know I mentioned that the weight of my heart is to put together a grill and break down the box.

1329
01:08:34.210 --> 01:08:44.850
But I think that if there was a guy that I actually was not that interested in, if he did this, I would be like, OK, all right.

1330
01:08:46.210 --> 01:08:47.950
It is so sweet.

1331
01:08:48.290 --> 01:08:50.070
It's so, so charming.

1332
01:08:50.510 --> 01:08:55.370
You know, my husband is a really good singer and he doesn't really sing around people.

1333
01:08:55.730 --> 01:09:02.030
But when we first started dating, we went out and there was karaoke and I didn't really know the side of him.

1334
01:09:02.190 --> 01:09:03.370
He's like an acapella guy.

1335
01:09:03.370 --> 01:09:08.890
And he got up and sang Journey and he brought down the bar.

1336
01:09:09.050 --> 01:09:11.310
And I was like, oh, my God.

1337
01:09:13.970 --> 01:09:17.650
But it was just so, so sweet in this moment.

1338
01:09:17.870 --> 01:09:20.750
Andy, you know, and Andy will go on to sing to Angela again.

1339
01:09:21.270 --> 01:09:26.030
But, you know, he must really like her if he's going to bust out the acapella group.

1340
01:09:26.650 --> 01:09:28.190
Yeah, he's all in.

1341
01:09:29.090 --> 01:09:31.670
I hope one of those guys was Broccoli Rob.

1342
01:09:31.930 --> 01:09:33.250
Oh, it had to have been.

1343
01:09:33.370 --> 01:09:33.930
Yeah.

1344
01:09:34.250 --> 01:09:39.350
And Angela just looks at him and says she has to go clean up the party.

1345
01:09:39.570 --> 01:09:44.150
And then we reveal that the whole bullpen has watched this.

1346
01:09:44.650 --> 01:09:44.850
Yeah.

1347
01:09:45.550 --> 01:09:46.470
Including Dwight.

1348
01:09:47.370 --> 01:09:47.690
Yeah.

1349
01:09:47.690 --> 01:09:54.390
And before we move on, Jenna, 38 minutes, 15 seconds.

1350
01:09:55.350 --> 01:09:57.170
Prime elbow poof.

1351
01:09:58.070 --> 01:10:00.330
Prime elbow poof of the sweater.

1352
01:10:00.610 --> 01:10:03.150
I don't even understand this sweater, you guys.

1353
01:10:03.350 --> 01:10:10.570
It was skinny at the top, then had a big floofy poofy part right at the elbow, then skinny again down to the wriSt.

1354
01:10:10.570 --> 01:10:14.490
And it also had lace sewn into the v-neck.

1355
01:10:15.930 --> 01:10:27.870
Yeah, I mean, I think that we have to acknowledge that Andy serenaded Angela while she was wearing this terrible blouse.

1356
01:10:29.050 --> 01:10:33.030
No other man was going to hit on Angela today.

1357
01:10:33.190 --> 01:10:33.590
Well.

1358
01:10:33.770 --> 01:10:37.550
I'll tell you that because that blouse is a repellent.

1359
01:10:38.110 --> 01:10:43.370
I think we have a callback to a flirty shade of beige here.

1360
01:10:43.530 --> 01:10:44.090
Yes.

1361
01:10:44.230 --> 01:10:46.230
Very flirty shade of beige again.

1362
01:10:46.230 --> 01:10:46.790
Yes.

1363
01:10:46.990 --> 01:10:51.530
Well, actually, it's like a Victorian shade of beige with the poofy sleeve, right?

1364
01:10:52.130 --> 01:10:52.390
Yeah.

1365
01:10:52.670 --> 01:10:53.450
The poofy elbow.

1366
01:10:53.450 --> 01:10:58.690
So, Dwight ogles her in this flirty shade of beige, and Andy sings to her.

1367
01:10:58.870 --> 01:11:00.810
So, clearly, something was working.

1368
01:11:02.010 --> 01:11:03.270
It's a shocker.

1369
01:11:05.630 --> 01:11:12.810
Well, now we go into Michael's office, and he and Dwight are just both miserable over this day.

1370
01:11:13.370 --> 01:11:15.030
Yeah, they've had a day.

1371
01:11:15.550 --> 01:11:22.570
And Michael says, more than anything, he's bummed that he did not get to have authentic New York sushi.

1372
01:11:22.830 --> 01:11:23.590
Not a thing.

1373
01:11:23.970 --> 01:11:24.310
Yeah.

1374
01:11:24.310 --> 01:11:26.430
New York has very good sushi.

1375
01:11:26.730 --> 01:11:27.030
Yeah.

1376
